regs->b0 = ((struct fnptr *)kretprobe_trampoline)->ip;
trampoline_p.addr = (kprobe_opcode_t *)((struct fnptr *)kretprobe_trampoline)->ip;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the code incorrectly passes the descriptor address of `kretprobe_trampoline` to the `__kretprobe_trampoline_handler()` instead of the actual function entry address. This misrepresentation leads to the handler executing at the wrong address, causing incorrect behavior in the kprobes functionality.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
regs->cr_iip = __kretprobe_trampoline_handler(regs, dereference_function_descriptor(kretprobe_trampoline), NULL);
regs->b0 = (unsigned long)dereference_function_descriptor(kretprobe_trampoline);
trampoline_p.addr = dereference_function_descriptor(kretprobe_trampoline);
```
Reason:
The fix involves using the `dereference_function_descriptor()` function to obtain the correct function entry address from `kretprobe_trampoline`. This ensures that the correct address is passed to the handler and used in other parts of the code, thereby restoring the intended functionality of the kprobes system.

